  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}$ using synthetic division.\n\nFor synthetic division to work, we need the coefficient of $x$ in the denominator to be equal to $1.$ So first, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1} & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}$, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 8 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & -4 & 0 & 1 \\\\  & 8 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}=4{x}^{2}-1.\n$$",
